{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Truly you are my very bone and flesh.</b> Even though you could sustain yourself without me through the work of shepherding or otherwise, nonetheless you are my very bone and flesh, and it is fitting that you dwell in my house." "<b>And he stayed with him.</b> In his service, tending his flock — as in <b>dwell with me</b>, and \"Moses consented to stay with the man\" (Exodus 2:21). Therefore he afterward said to him, <b>and you shall serve me for nothing</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:18.924988657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}